### Phase 1 completion gate

- [x] A controlled scheduler can drive pointer samples without creating or
      retaining UI objects.
- [x] Exactly one pointer read and one observer notification occur per active
      tick.
- [x] Stop and reload make every previously queued callback inert.
- [x] Focused poller and package-contract tests pass.

### Phase 1 evidence

- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/pointer_poller.lua` exports the documented
  `PointerPoller` contract through the normal DFHack script environment. Its
  default collaborators schedule one frame through `dfhack.timeout()` and
  perform one `dfhack.screen.getMousePos()` call. Injected scheduler, sampler,
  observer, and demand collaborators keep focused tests independent of GUI,
  overlay, tooltip, and renderer modules.
- Instance-generation tokens invalidate stop/restart callbacks, and the
  process-wide module generation in `dfhack.dwarfui` invalidates callbacks
  from cleared script environments. The stale-callback test executes an old
  callback before a restarted chain and proves it cannot stop or duplicate the
  newer chain.
- `tests/pointer_poller.spec.lua` covers start, duplicate start, immutable
  sample publication, missing-coordinate normalization, one read and one
  notification per tick, monotonic sequence values, idempotent stop, stale
  instance callbacks, demand loss before sampling and after observation,
  observer failure, deliberate restart, module reload, production defaults,
  and dependency isolation.
- Focused poller, module-registry, and package-contract tests reported
  `23 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`. The complete standalone suite
  reported `194 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`.
- Lua 5.4.6 syntax validation passed for 17 production and 35 test/support
  files. Unit-test naming, the non-live build, and `git diff --check` passed.
- Package publication and verification passed for both expanded and zip
  artifacts. Both contained
  `scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/pointer_poller.lua`; the task-owned temporary
  package directory was removed after verification.
- No live reload or DwarfSpec run was required by the Phase 1 gate and none is
  counted as Phase 1 evidence.

## Phase 2: Extract tooltip target detection

- [x] Move registration-root discovery, root eligibility, and cross-root
      target arbitration out of the current screen-owned update path.
- [x] Implement a documented detector that accepts one `PointerSample` and
      returns one `TooltipPointerObservation`.
- [x] Keep the existing `PointerDispatcher.resolve()` implementation as the
      within-root hit-testing authority.
- [x] Preserve weak registrations and registration sequence without retaining
      widgets in poller-owned state.
- [x] Resolve each distinct eligible root at most once per sample.
- [x] Preserve target-local coordinates returned by the pointer dispatcher.
- [x] Produce explicit `target`, `blocked`, and `miss` observations.
- [x] Make a no-pointer sample produce a `miss` without running hit tests.
- [x] Isolate cross-root arbitration behind one documented policy function.
- [x] Remove every dependency from detection to `TooltipRenderer`,
      `gui.ZScreen`, rendering bounds, renderer visibility, and presentation
      refresh.
- [x] Add focused detector coverage for detached controls, invisible or
      inactive ancestors, stale overlay instances, disabled overlays,
      viewscreen mismatch, native-mounted roots, overlapping subviews,
      blocked regions, unregistered resolved controls, overlapping roots, and
      no-pointer samples.
- [x] Add a test proving one sample cannot notify two registered controls even
      when their roots overlap.

### Phase 2 completion gate

- [x] Detection is deterministic for target, blocked, and miss results.
- [x] Eligibility and arbitration operate without creating or querying a
      tooltip presentation host.
- [x] The detector performs no pointer callbacks and reads no tooltip text.
- [x] Focused pointer and detector tests pass.

### Phase 2 evidence

- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/tooltip_target_detector.lua` owns attached
  registration-root discovery, ancestor eligibility, overlay/native
  presentation predicates, one-resolution-per-root hit testing, and
  registration-sequence arbitration. Its only module dependencies are
  `plugins.overlay` and `dwarfui/pointer`; it has no tooltip renderer,
  `gui.ZScreen`, layout-presentation, refresh, or pointer-callback dependency.
- `tooltip_registration.lua` now constructs a `PointerSample`, asks the
  detector for one `TooltipPointerObservation`, and retains only the temporary
  callback and renderer mediation that later phases will replace. The former
  screen-owned discovery, eligibility, and arbitration functions were removed.
- `tests/tooltip_target_detector.spec.lua` covers presentation dependency
  isolation, detached and stale attachment, invisible and inactive
  descendants/ancestors, missing layout, disabled/stale/mismatched overlays,
  current native-root identity, overlapping subviews, target-local
  coordinates, blocked regions, unregistered resolved controls, overlapping
  roots, deterministic target and blocked arbitration, one resolution per
  root, no-pointer short-circuiting, weak registration ownership, and the
  absence of tooltip reads or pointer callbacks.
- Focused pointer, detector, registration, registry, and package-contract tests
  reported `55 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`. The complete standalone
  suite reported `209 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`.
- Lua 5.4.6 syntax validation passed for 18 production and 36 test/support
  files. Unit-test naming, the non-live build, and `git diff --check` passed.
- Expanded and zip package verification passed, and the published manifest
  contained `scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/tooltip_target_detector.lua`. The
  task-owned temporary package directory was removed after verification.
- A live `dwarfui reload` completed successfully with the detector ordered
  between pointer acquisition/resolution and tooltip-registration consumers.

## Phase 3: Convert the tooltip service to observation and intent mediation

- [x] Give the process-wide tooltip service one documented
      `accept_pointer_observation(observation)` entrypoint.
- [x] Move current-target ownership and pointer transition callbacks into that
      entrypoint.
- [x] Preserve leave-before-enter ordering when the winning target changes.
- [x] Run `on_pointer_update` after any enter callback and before reading
      tooltip text.
- [x] Preserve the validation rule that tooltip values are strings, `nil`, or
      empty strings.
- [x] Treat `nil` and empty strings as no current intent without losing the
      current hover target.
- [x] Snapshot nonempty tooltip text into a new immutable intent with the
      sample's screen-cell pointer coordinates as its anchor.
- [x] Increment the intent revision on every publish and clear operation that
      changes observable service state.
- [x] Reject or ignore out-of-order observations whose sample sequence is
      older than the last accepted sequence.
- [x] Expose current intent and revision through diagnostics without exposing
      a renderer or screen.
- [x] Define a presentation-neutral intent observer boundary and make absence
      of an observer valid.
- [x] Ensure observer replacement or removal cannot synthesize pointer enter,
      leave, or update callbacks.
- [x] Clear intent and deliver one leave callback when the active registration
      is removed, collected, detached, or becomes ineligible.
- [x] Clear intent and target state during deliberate shutdown and
      same-version reload.
- [x] Replace direct renderer mutation in the input path with intent
      publication.
- [x] Add focused service coverage for initial target, repeated update,
      target transition, blocked and miss clearing, dynamic text, empty text,
      invalid text, stale observation, unregister, collection, shutdown,
      reload, missing consumer, and consumer replacement.
- [x] Add a dependency-isolation test proving the service's input path can load
      and run with no tooltip renderer or `gui.ZScreen` implementation.

### Phase 3 completion gate

- [x] Pointer callbacks and tooltip text snapshots match the established
      behavior.
- [x] The service publishes only text, anchor, coordinate space, and revision
      data required by a future presenter.
- [x] Target loss clears intent immediately and exactly once.
- [x] No input-path module imports or calls a tooltip renderer.
- [x] Focused tooltip service tests pass.

### Phase 3 evidence

- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/tooltip_service.lua` exports the documented
  `TooltipService` class and one process-wide `service` instance. The instance
  owns its reload-safe state through `self` and mediates weak registrations,
  current-target transitions, tooltip validation, immutable `TooltipIntent`
  snapshots, monotonically increasing revisions, observation ordering, intent
  observation, shutdown, and reload cleanup. The module imports no GUI,
  overlay, tooltip renderer, ZScreen, or presentation module.
- The service's diagnostics expose generation, registration count, target,
  intent, revision, and accepted sequence without exposing a renderer, screen,
  overlay, painter, frame, or rendering bounds. Intent snapshots contain only
  text, anchor coordinates, screen-cell coordinate space, revision/source
  sequence, and the opaque source root required by the confirmed contract.
- At the Phase 3 checkpoint, `tooltip_registration.lua` sent detector
  observations to `accept_pointer_observation()` while its temporary legacy
  ZScreen remained the presentation consumer. Phase 4 removes that consumer
  and supersedes this historical checkpoint.
- `tests/tooltip_service.spec.lua` covers initial and repeated dynamic intent,
  immutability, callback order, target transitions, blocked and miss clearing,
  nil/empty/invalid text, stale and duplicate observations, unregister,
  weak-registration collection and collected-entry loss, ineligibility,
  missing/replaced/removed consumers, idempotent shutdown, same-version reload,
  legacy-state migration, version conflicts, clean diagnostics, and loading
  with no presentation implementation.
- Focused service, registration, detector, registry, and package-contract tests
  reported `58 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`. The complete standalone
  suite reported `227 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`.
- Lua 5.4.6 syntax validation passed for 19 production and 37 test/support
  files. Unit-test naming, the non-live build, and `git diff --check` passed.
- Expanded and zip package verification passed, and the published manifest
  contained `scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/tooltip_service.lua`. The task-owned
  temporary package directory was removed after verification.
- Two live `dwarfui reload` commands completed successfully and exercised
  same-version target, intent, observer, and ordering cleanup.

## Phase 4: Wire registration demand to polling lifecycle

- [x] Start the singleton poller when the first live tooltip registration is
      created.
- [x] Preserve idempotent duplicate registration.
- [x] Keep the poller running while at least one live weak registration
      remains, including when all current roots are temporarily ineligible.
- [x] Stop the poller after explicit removal or collection of the final
      registration.
- [x] Make a no-registration reload leave no active or resuming timeout chain.
- [x] Make a same-version reload with live registrations retire the old
      generation and start exactly one new generation.
- [x] Remove screen creation, screen resumption, raising, dismissal, and
      special native-screen lists from the registration lifecycle.
- [x] Do not add map-load gating as a substitute for correct lifecycle
      isolation.
- [x] Extend diagnostics with poller generation, running state, scheduled
      state, sample sequence, target, current intent, and registration count.
- [x] Remove diagnostics whose only meaning was a service screen or renderer
      count from production code and input-layer tests in this phase.
- [x] Update the module registry and reload ordering so the poller, pointer
      resolver, detector, and tooltip service are rebuilt as one coherent
      generation.
- [x] Add focused lifecycle coverage for zero-to-one, one-to-many,
      many-to-one, and one-to-zero registrations; collection; reload; and
      repeated reload.

### Phase 4 completion gate

- [x] Registrations control exactly one process-wide polling chain.
- [x] No tooltip registration creates or manipulates a DFHack screen or
      overlay.
- [x] Repeated `dwarfui reload` leaves one current generation and no callbacks
      capable of reviving an older generation.
- [x] Focused registration, registry, and reload tests pass.

### Phase 4 evidence

- `tooltip_registration.lua` now creates one `PointerPoller` for the current
  coherent module generation. Registration demand starts and stops that chain;
  each sample flows through `TooltipTargetDetector` and then
  `TooltipService:accept_pointer_observation()` without importing GUI,
  renderer, overlay-host, focus, input, or map-load lifecycle code.
- `PointerPoller:get_diagnostics()` and the registration diagnostics expose
  module/instance generation, current/running/scheduled state, sample sequence,
  registration count, target, and intent. Screen and renderer-count
  diagnostics were removed.
- Focused poller, detector, service, registration, registry, reload-command,
  and package-contract tests reported
  `62 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`. The complete standalone suite
  reported `218 successes / 0 failures / 0 errors`.
- Lua 5.4.6 syntax validation passed for 19 production and 37 test/support
  files. Unit-test naming, the non-live build, and `git diff --check` passed.
- Expanded and zip package verification passed. The manifest contained
  `pointer.lua`, `pointer_poller.lua`, `tooltip_target_detector.lua`,
  `tooltip_service.lua`, and `tooltip_registration.lua` in the expected
  package, and the packaged registration source contained no ZScreen,
  renderer, state-change, or map-load dependency. The temporary package
  directory was removed.
- The existing focused minecart tooltip automation passed through the
  unchanged thin runner with `cleanup_confirmed=true`; it observed the
  production zoom action's `Zoom to this stop` intent and current poller
  state without asserting visual rendering.
- Consecutive live `dwarfui reload` commands left the native dwarfmode
  viewscreen topmost, one live registration, and exactly one current, running,
  scheduled poller generation. The module generation advanced once per reload
  and the new sample sequence continued advancing.

## Phase 5: Add live automation for input independence

- [ ] Add a focused `.ds.lua` test whose filename ends only in `.ds.lua`.
- [ ] Use the actual registered minecart overlay and its real zoom button as
      the tooltip target.
- [ ] Open the native Hauling menu through public DwarfSpec input APIs.
- [ ] Move the pointer through DwarfSpec onto the rendered production zoom
      button without calling detector, service-update, render, or input methods
      directly.
- [ ] Await diagnostics that identify the production button as the current
      target and report the exact text `Zoom to this stop`.
- [ ] Assert the published anchor equals the sampled screen-cell pointer
      position.
- [ ] Move within the button and prove target-local update can change dynamic
      tooltip text before the service snapshots it.
- [ ] Move off the button and prove the intent clears and the leave callback
      occurs without synthetic input.
- [ ] Place an input-consuming widget in the normal dispatch path and prove
      pointer polling still updates the target and intent.
- [ ] Assert DwarfSpec's focus string and current native viewscreen are
      unchanged by registration, pointer movement, intent publication, and
      target clearing.
- [ ] Assert polling diagnostics expose no screen, overlay, renderer, or input
      ownership created by the input subsystem.
- [ ] Run `dwarfui reload` with a live registration and prove sampling resumes
      through one new generation without duplicate callbacks or a lost
      Hauling overlay.
- [ ] Close and reopen the Hauling menu and prove temporarily ineligible
      registrations neither publish stale intent nor require re-registration.
- [ ] Include a safe title/load/map transition probe if Phase 0 confirms that
      it can be automated without modifying the prepared save.
- [ ] Restore pointer position, native menu state, scroll position, focus,
      mounted subjects, and all test-owned registrations even when an
      assertion fails.
- [ ] Require `cleanup_confirmed=true` and zero retained DwarfSpec screens,
      subjects, and pointer ownership.

### Phase 5 completion gate

- [ ] Real pointer movement selects and clears the real minecart zoom tooltip
      target through the polling path.
- [ ] An input consumer cannot prevent the polling path from observing hover.
- [ ] Focus, native viewscreen identity, pause state, and input routing remain
      unchanged.
- [ ] Reload leaves exactly one live poller generation and the registered
      Hauling overlay remains available.
- [ ] Focused live automation passes with confirmed cleanup.

