- [ ] Run Lua syntax validation for production, test, and support sources.
- [ ] Run unit-test naming validation.
- [ ] Run package verification and inspect the packaged script manifest for
      every new production module.
- [ ] Run the focused DwarfSpec input-polling test through the unchanged thin
      `Tools/Run-AutomationTests.ps1` pass-through.
- [ ] Run the existing native minecart interaction tests to detect registration
      or reload regressions.
- [ ] Run the focused live proof twice to detect leaked timeout generations.
- [ ] Record focused, full-suite, syntax, naming, package, live, repeat-run, and
      cleanup evidence separately.
- [ ] Do not count a published intent as proof that a tooltip is visually
      rendered.
- [ ] Produce the rendering plan against the stable `TooltipIntent` boundary
      without revising pointer acquisition or target detection.

### Phase 6 completion gate

- [ ] All focused and complete verification categories pass.
- [ ] Package contents include the poller and detector modules in valid reload
      order.
- [ ] Live evidence proves input independence and lifecycle invisibility.
- [ ] No rendering claim is made until the separate rendering plan is
      implemented and verified.

## Planned file impact

Expected production changes:

- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/pointer_poller.lua` — generic recurring
  pointer acquisition.
- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/pointer.lua` — retain the generic resolver;
  adjust only if observation extraction requires a presentation-independent
  helper.
- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/tooltip_registration.lua` — weak
  registrations, target detection, observation mediation, intent publication,
  polling demand, diagnostics, and reload lifecycle.
- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/tooltip.lua` — public registration and
  intent-facing API cleanup; renderer code remains outside the polling path.
- `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/module_registry.lua` — dependency and
  reload ordering.

Expected test changes:

- `tests/pointer_poller.spec.lua`
- `tests/pointer.spec.lua`
- `tests/tooltip_registration.spec.lua`
- `tests/module_registry.spec.lua`
- `tests/package_contract.spec.lua`
- `tests/minecart_route/minecart_route_tooltip.ds.lua`

The exact live-test filename may change if keeping polling evidence separate
from the later rendering evidence produces a clearer DwarfSpec contract.

## Rendering-plan handoff contract

The later rendering plan may depend only on:

- a current `TooltipIntent` or clear notification,
- monotonically increasing intent revisions,
- text already validated and snapshotted,
- an anchor in documented screen-cell coordinates, and
- the opaque source root already identified during hit testing, and
- optional lifecycle diagnostics that do not expose input internals.

It may not require the poller or detector to:

- create a presentation surface,
- calculate a tooltip frame or wrapped dimensions,
- request z-order or focus,
- forward or consume input,
- know which rendering technology is selected, or
- change its polling cadence to make rendering occur.
